{
 "title": "Selecting and Testing Asset Pricing Models: A Stepwise Approach (Management Science, first draft Apr 2023 this draft Jan 2026)",
 "hypothesis": "Optimal 8-factor model spans joint efficient frontier of test assets and all candidate factors: SR2(f_SEL)=SR2(r,F) equivalently alpha_tilde(M)=0 for LHS unselected factors and unselected candidate factors enhance test assets (reject implicit SR2(r)=SR2(r,f_UNS))",
 "data_sources": [
  "97 factor returns (FF6, Q5, DHS3, BS6, BAB, QMJ, BETA, LTR, STR, LIQ, VOL, IMD, SUE, NI, S^PLS, plus 74 HXZ factors) from authors websites and Lu Zhang website",
  "285 bivariate-sorted basis portfolios (25 size-BM, 25 size-OP, 25 size-INV, 25 size-MOM, 25 size-beta, 25 size-STR, 25 size-LTR, 25 size-var, 25 size-resvar, 35 size-NSI, 25 size-accruals) from Ken French website",
  "Sentiment S^PLS from Huang et al.2015 website for high/low sentiment split"
 ],
 "sample": "monthly U.S. equity returns of 97 traded candidate factors and 285 bivariate-sorted basis portfolios, seven baseline models CAPM(1) FF3(3) FF5(5) FF6(6) Q5(5) DHS3(3) BS6(6), expanded efficient models (CAPM^F 8, FF3^F 11, FF5^F 11, FF6^F 12, Q5^F 10, DHS3^F 9, BS6^F 12) and reduced optimal 8-factor model M8 = MKT REG PEAD HMLM STR ILR SMB EPRD, 588 months, factors one-month holding period, portfolio returns value-weighted, factors as long-short decile spreads",
 "period_start": "January 1973",
 "period_end": "December 2021",
 "method": [
  "1. Data: construct 97 factor returns F_t, 285 basis portfolio returns R_t, baseline models M_b subsets of F (e.g., CAPM {MKT}); sample T=588 months Jan 1973-Dec 2021, one-month holding, excess returns in %.",
  "2. Spanning regression for any candidate model M: F_tilde(M)_t = alpha_tilde(M) + beta_tilde(M)' F(M)_t + eps_tilde(M)_t, where tilde(M)=F\\M size N-|M| are LHS unselected candidate factors (and optionally 285 basis portfolios), RHS=M. Estimate by OLS per LHS asset.",
  "3. Model comparison: compute GRS(M)= (T-N)/(N-|M|) * ((1+SR2{F})/(1+SR2{F(M)}) -1) ~ F(N-|M|, T-N) under H0, and equivalently SR2{M}=mu_M' Sigma_M^{-1} mu_M, GRS decrease = SR2 increase * constant; maximal SR2 increment from adding factor j is alpha_j^2/sigma_eps,jj. HDA(M)= [T * alpha_hat' Diag(Sigma_eps_hat)^{-1} alpha_hat/(1+SR2{M}) - N1] / sqrt(2 N1[1+(N1-1) rho_hat^2]) -> N(0,1) under H0, N1=N-|M|, rho_hat sparsity correction; reject H0: alpha_tilde=0 if GRS p<0.05 or HDA>z_lambda with z_0.05=1.645 parameter.",
  "4. Forward Stepwise Evaluation (FSE) expansion: initialize S(0)=M_b. For k=1 to N-|M_b|-1 enumerate all J=N-|S(k-1)| one-factor expansions M_j(k-1)=S(k-1) U {j}, estimate spanning regression of F_tilde(M_j) on F(M_j), compute GRS(M_j) (Eq GRS_j) and SR2{F(M_j)}; pick a_k = argmin GRS = argmax SR2; update S(k)=S(k-1)U{a_k}; compute HDA{S(k)}; stop when HDA<z_lambda (fail to reject) at k_hat, return M_b^F=S(k_hat). Guarantees screening consistency P(T subset M_b^F)->1, |M_b^F|=O(N^{n1+2n2}) with N^{1+n2} log N=o(T).",
  "5. Backward Stepwise Evaluation (BSE) reduction: initialize S(0)=M_b^F efficient large model. For m=1 to |M_b^F|-1 enumerate all J=|S(m-1)| one-factor reductions M_j(m-1)=S(m-1)\\{j}, compute GRS and SR2, pick b_m = argmin GRS = argmax SR2; update S(m)=S(m-1)\\{b_m}; compute HDA{S(m)}; stop when HDA>z_lambda (reject) at m_hat, return M_b^{F+B}=S(m_hat-1). Guarantees selection consistency P(M_b^{F+B}=T)->1 if sqrt(N) log N <~ z^2 <~ T N^{-1/2-n2}.",
  "6. Performance evaluation: asset pricing A|alpha|=N^{-1} sum|alpha_i|, A|t(alpha)|, #sign2 = sum I(|t|>1.96) tally, Total R2 =1- sum sum (R_it - beta_i' f_t)^2 / sum sum (R_it - CAPM_fit)^2, CS R2 =1- sum (R_bar_i - beta_i' lambda)^2 / sum (R_bar_i - CAPM_ER)^2; investment AVG, Ann.SR = sqrt(12)* mean/std of tangency portfolio (max SR2)^{1/2}, alpha_CAPM and alpha_FF5 from time-series regression of tangency on benchmark.",
  "7. Out-of-sample: split 588 months into 3 sequential folds Time1 1973/01-1989/04 (196), Time2 1989/05-2005/08 (196), Time3 2005/09-2021/12 (196); for each fold train on other 392 months to select M^{F+B} and estimate mean/Sigma and tangency weights, apply to test 196 months constant, report INS/OOS Total/CS R2 and Ann.SR; bootstrap INS vs OOS SR2: split into 294 adjacent month-pairs (1,2)...(587,588), each bootstrap randomly assign one of pair to INS other to OOS, draw 294 pairs with replacement, 1000 replications parameter, compute INS SR2 and OOS SR2 with INS weights, report M-SR2 average, pairwise outperformance probability % and Best %.",
  "8. Robustness: subtract transaction costs from factor returns before evaluation: 2 bps/month for annually rebalanced factors (MKT buy-hold 0, SMB, EPRD), 12 or 24 bps/month for monthly rebalanced (REG PEAD HMLM STR ILR); repeat FSE/BSE; individual factor test: for each row factor form baseline MKT+row (96) or FF3+row (94) 2- or 4-factor baseline, run FSE to efficient then BSE to optimal, record if row factor survives in reduced model and selection rate."
 ],
